fpga-shells: arty_a7_200 entry in the write_cfgmem board table.

write_cfgmem.tcl looks the board up in ::program::boards::spec, which
boards.tcl rebuilds whenever it is sourced, so an entry cannot be added from
outside without replacing the script. The arty_a7_200 board directory itself
comes from RiskyBird's overlay (hardware/fpga-shells/xilinx/arty_a7_200): a
TE0712 with the XC7A200T and the 32 MiB S25FL256S configuration flash. This
is the RiskyBird fork's entry with one correction: iface spix1, not spix4.
The board's bitstreams are SPIx1 (hardware/fpga-shells/xilinx/arty_a7_200/
constraints/arty-config.xdc: the flash's QUAD bit is clear), and write_cfgmem
refuses an SPIx4 configuration-memory file for them ([Writecfgmem 68-20]
SPI_BUSWIDTH is "1"). Drop it if the board ever lands in fpga-shells upstream
with its own entry.

diff --git a/xilinx/common/tcl/boards.tcl b/xilinx/common/tcl/boards.tcl
index c3ffc1f..0ef2c77 100644
--- a/xilinx/common/tcl/boards.tcl
+++ b/xilinx/common/tcl/boards.tcl
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@ namespace eval ::program::boards {}
 set ::program::boards::spec [dict create \
 	arty            [dict create  iface spix4   size 16   bitaddr 0x0        memdev {n25q128-3.3v-spi-x1_x2_x4}] \
 	arty_a7_100     [dict create  iface spix4   size 16   bitaddr 0x0        memdev {s25fl128sxxxxxx0-spi-x1_x2_x4}] \
+	arty_a7_200     [dict create  iface spix1   size 32   bitaddr 0x0        memdev {s25fl256sxxxxxx0-spi-x1_x2_x4}] \
 	nexys_video     [dict create  iface spix4   size 32   bitaddr 0x0        memdev {s25fl256sxxxxxx0-spi-x1_x2_x4}] \
 	vc707           [dict create  iface bpix16  size 128  bitaddr 0x3000000  ] \
 	vcu118          [dict create  iface spix8   size 256  bitaddr 0x0        memdev {mt25qu01g-spi-x1_x2_x4_x8}]]
